From faccf9f515bc5ccb326c9f2ab6279a6ba3d2c3f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:37:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Fixes found running the examples: maps, exports, checks
 with a saved ds_solar

- topo_plot.map_variable and map_clusters: the points of the zarr store carry
  x, y and elevation coordinates, which clashed with the grid of ds_param
  (IndexError). They are dropped before mapping the points to the grid.
- Topoclass.plot.map_clusters called a function of topo_param; load_project
  now also gives the plotting helper ds_param and the downscaled points.
- topo_sub.plot_center_clusters (Topoclass.toposub.plot_clusters_map) and
  write_landform: cluster labels are stored as point names ('00', '-9999'),
  which could not be multiplied by the hillshade or written as integers.
- to_cryogrid, to_crocus and to_surfex read latitude and longitude, which a
  list of points may hold but df_centroids of TopoSUB does not (lat, lon).
- The physics checks compute the solar geometry from the coordinates of the
  points when they can, as the downscaling does, and use a saved ds_solar
  only otherwise, if it holds the points: a ds_solar saved before the points
  changed raised a KeyError after downscaling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
